      "text": "The given equation of the hyperbola is \\(\\frac{y^2}{27} - \\frac{x^2}{11} = 1\\). For a hyperbola of the form \\(\\frac{y^2}{a^2} - \\frac{x^2}{b^2} = 1\\), the distance between the vertices is \\(2a\\). Here, \\(a^2 = 27\\), so \\(a = \\sqrt{27} = 3\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nTherefore, the distance between the vertices is \\(2a = 2 \\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\na_squared = 27\n\n# Calculate a\na = math.sqrt(a_squared)\n\n# Distance between the vertices\ndistance_between_vertices = 2 * a\nprint(distance_between_vertices)\n```\n```output\n10.392304845413264\n```\nThe distance between the vertices of the hyperbola \\(\\frac{y^2}{27} - \\frac{x^2}{11} = 1\\) is \\(6\\sqrt{3}\\), which is approximately 10.392.\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\\).",
